---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import DeployButton from '../components/DeployButton.astro';
import snippets from '../../../../docs/onboarding/snippets.json';
import {installShell,installNpm} from '../lib/links.mjs';
const sections=[{id:'deploy',label:'Deploy'},{id:'install',label:'Install & connect'},{id:'capture',label:'Capture'},{id:'sync',label:'Sync'},{id:'agent',label:'Agent'},{id:'report',label:'Report'}];
---
<Page title="Quickstart" description="Deploy your own Slurp Worker on Cloudflare, connect the CLI, capture events, sync to DuckDB, and give your agent local data." current="docs" sections={sections}>
<header class="docs-intro"><p class="eyebrow">Quickstart</p><h1>Start collecting events.</h1><p class="lede">Deploy a Worker to your own Cloudflare account, connect the CLI, and keep your events in one local database. Install the CLI with one command, on macOS or Linux.</p></header>
<section class="section" id="deploy"><span class="section-number">00 / DEPLOY</span><h2>Put the Worker in your account.</h2><p>Deploy one Worker, two Durable Object classes and an R2 bucket into your own Cloudflare account. Cloudflare creates the resources and asks you to set an <code>ADMIN_TOKEN</code>. Generate one with <code>openssl rand -base64 32</code> and save it in your password manager.</p><div class="actions"><DeployButton id="docs"/><a class="btn" href="/self-host/">Cost and limits</a></div><p>When deployment finishes, open your Worker’s address. It shows the command to connect this computer. Prefer the terminal? <a href="#terminal-deploy">Deploy with the CLI instead.</a></p></section>
<section class="section" id="install"><span class="section-number">01 / INSTALL & CONNECT</span><h2>Make a home for your events.</h2><p>Install the CLI with the shell command or npm. <code>slurp cloud init</code> deploys your Worker and connects this computer to it. Already have one? <code>slurp connect &lt;url&gt; --token-stdin</code> checks its admin token and remembers it. Setup finds DuckDB or offers to install it. Init creates or selects an app by name. Run <code>slurp projects</code> to list registered projects.</p><Code label="Terminal" code={`${installShell}
# or: ${installNpm}
slurp connect https://slurp.YOUR-SUBDOMAIN.workers.dev --token-stdin
slurp setup
cd /path/to/your/app
slurp init --name "My app"`}/><p class="fine">Paste the admin token into standard input when connecting; finish with Control-D. Keep it out of the command itself.</p><details id="terminal-deploy"><summary>Deploy from your terminal instead</summary><p>You need Node 20+ and a Cloudflare account. This command deploys and connects your Worker:</p><Code label="Terminal" code="slurp cloud init"/></details><p><code>slurp init</code> opens a private offline quickstart with your project’s SDK instructions. Rerun init to refresh that page.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="capture"><span class="section-number">02 / CAPTURE</span><h2>Send your first event.</h2><p>The SDK is private until published. For development, build it and install the local package into your application:</p><Code label="Terminal" code={`pnpm install
pnpm --filter @slurp/sdk build
# In your application:
npm install /absolute/path/to/this/repository/packages/sdk-js`}/><p>Replace the placeholders with values in your private project quickstart. Publishable keys are ingest-only.</p><Code label="JavaScript / Node" code={snippets.sdk}/><h3>Test from your terminal.</h3><p>Inside your app or a subfolder, Slurp uses the nearest project binding and its saved SDK key.</p><Code label="Your app folder" code={`slurp send signed_up --user-id demo_alice --data '{"demo":true}'
slurp sync`}/><p class="fine">Sending confirms durable acceptance. Events appear in <code>slurp sync</code> after your Worker next seals an archive, about every 10 minutes by default (earlier when a batch reaches 8 MB).</p><h3 id="http">Send events over HTTP.</h3><p>Any language can POST canonical events as newline-delimited JSON to <code>/v1/events</code> on your Worker. Use <code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_PUBLISHABLE_KEY</code> and <code>Content-Type: application/x-ndjson</code>. Tool-specific webhook payloads need translation into this format.</p><Code label="One NDJSON record (end with a newline)" code={'{"id":"YOUR_UNIQUE_EVENT_ID","type":"track","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:00:00Z","event":"signed_up","data":{"plan":"pro"}}'}/><p class="fine">A successful response means durable acceptance. Retrying the exact same bytes is safe: the Worker answers with <code>Slurp-Duplicate: 1</code> and local import ignores repeated event IDs.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="sync"><span class="section-number">03 / SYNC</span><h2>Bring the events home.</h2><Code label="Terminal · your workspace" code={snippets.sync}/><p>Run <code>slurp sync</code> to download new archives from your Worker into your local DuckDB database. Recently accepted events may still be waiting for the next seal. Close open DuckDB sessions before syncing.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="agent"><span class="section-number">04 / AGENT</span><h2>Give your agent the context.</h2><Code label="Install the skill bundle" code="slurp agent setup --out .agents/skills/slurp --all"/><p>Ask your local coding agent to inspect the workspace and query its events. For a bot running on another machine, create a separate revocable read key:</p><Code label="Create bot access" code={snippets.key}/><p>Transfer the returned key through the bot’s secret store as <code>SLURP_TOKEN</code>, then run these steps on its machine:</p><Code label="Bot machine" code={snippets.agent}/><p class="fine">Keep keys out of URLs, reports, and skill files. Revoke a key with <code>slurp source key revoke</code>.</p></section>
<section class="section" id="report"><span class="section-number">05 / REPORT</span><h2>Keep the query with the finding.</h2><p>Ask your agent to create <code>report.md</code> using the repository’s <code>examples/events.md</code> as a reference. Reports combine Markdown, named SQL queries, and metric, table, or chart blocks.</p><Code label="Validate, build, open" code={`slurp report check report.md
slurp report build report.md --out ./report --png --pdf
slurp report open ./report`}/><p>HTML embeds charts and fonts. PNG and PDF are ready to share. Review the included data before sharing a report.</p></section>
</Page>

<style>.docs-intro{padding-bottom:40px;max-width:740px}.docs-intro h1{font-size:clamp(36px,4vw,50px)}.section h3{margin-top:36px}.section details{padding:16px 0;border-block:1px solid var(--rule);margin:24px 0}.section summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;font-weight:600}</style>
